# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Arduino build output. The linker artefacts are regenerable and large, but the
# plain .hex is kept: it is exactly what is flashed to the boards, so a
# replacement Mega can be programmed with avrdude alone, without installing the
# whole toolchain first.
IODebug/build/*
!IODebug/build/arduino.avr.mega/
IODebug/build/arduino.avr.mega/*
!IODebug/build/arduino.avr.mega/IODebug.ino.hex

# Per-lift firmware: keep the exact image flashed to each board, drop the rest.
# Lift identity is compiled in, so these are NOT interchangeable between lifts.
firmware/*/*
!firmware/*/IODebug.ino.hex
# firmware/docs is documentation, not a build directory - the pattern above
# swallowed it by accident.
!firmware/docs/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything developed here is published - nothing in this project is secret
# (user decision, 13 Sep 2026). What remains ignored is only what would do
# harm, or is regenerated automatically, if it reached another machine:
#   __pycache__/ *.pyc and the IODebug linker intermediates (top of this file)
#   are rebuilt on every run or compile; the flashed .hex images are kept.

# Runtime control flag for log_lift.py. Committed, it would stop every
# capture on any machine that pulls the repo.
STOP_CAPTURE

# Live process handles written by running loggers. On another machine - or on
# this one after a reboot - the pid names an unrelated process, and the
# watchdog would then believe that lift is already being captured and skip it.
capture_lift_*.pid

# (vendor/, capture_launcher.log and the diagnostic outputs used to be ignored;
# they are work products and are now published.)
